## Add a "No Backend" (ontology-only) domain type

Context: Some domains only need to publish their ontology, with no Knowledge
Graph. Introduce a per-domain graph backend value "none" that disables all
graph tooling: the Mapping and Knowledge Graph navbar features are turned off,
the graph MCP tools are unselected and force-disabled (leaving only
describe_ontology), and a habilitated user can move such a domain to IN-REVIEW
and PUBLISHED on the strength of its ontology alone, with no build. The
standalone MCP server needs no change: it already hides graph tools via the
persisted policy, so an ontology-only domain serves only ontology information.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   Added "none" to GRAPH_BACKENDS with a GRAPHLESS_BACKEND constant and an
   is_graphless_backend() helper; _create_auto now returns None (no store) for
   a graphless domain.
2. src/back/core/mcp_tools.py
   Tagged each domain tool with requires_graph, exposed MCP_GRAPH_TOOL_NAMES,
   and added force_graphless_policy() to disable every graph tool in a policy.
3. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   save_domain_info now force-disables the graph MCP tools whenever the domain
   backend is "none", independent of the client payload.
4. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Documented "none" as a valid per-domain graph backend.
5. src/back/objects/registry/ReviewService.py
   Relaxed can_submit / submit_blocked_reason (review_detail) and the My Tasks
   worklist (_pending_actions) so a No Backend domain submits on its ontology
   alone; graph-backed domains still require a build.
6. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   Surfaced per-version graph_backend and has_ontology in the cached metadata
   so the worklist can gate submission without extra reads.
7. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   Added the "No Backend" option, an ontology-only notice, and a
   data-requires-graph marker on each MCP tool checkbox.
8. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   Added applyGraphlessConstraints() to uncheck + lock the graph MCP tools and
   reveal the notice for a No Backend domain, wired on change/init/rehydrate.
9. src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js
   Re-applied the graphless lock after an MCP policy rehydrate and stopped
   "select all" from re-checking a locked tool.
10. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
    Added updateMenusForGraphBackend() to disable the Mapping and Knowledge
    Graph navigation for a No Backend domain.
11. src/front/templates/base.html
    Marked the Mapping and Knowledge Graph subnav tabs with nav-requires-graph.
12. src/front/routes/mapping.py, src/front/routes/dtwin.py
    Redirected a No Backend domain away from the Mapping and Knowledge Graph
    pages (direct-URL hardening).
13. tests/units/graphdb/test_graphless_backend.py,
    tests/units/core/test_mcp_graphless_policy.py,
    tests/units/registry/test_review_service.py,
    tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py,
    tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_triple_store_backend_config.py
    Covered the vocabulary, forced policy, review-gate relaxation, and the
    frontend contracts; updated the allowed-backends assertion.

